00:00:01.750 --> 00:00:03.830 align:start position:0%
it's been more than three years since  the horrific events of one october  but the fbi is still working to give  closure to survivors who were at the  route 91 harvest music festival  personal items left at the concert  grounds that night need to be returned  bianca holman explains the healing  garden is a place for peace  and reflection there are many items here  from those that were taken from us that  night but for those living they've yet  to receive those items left behind  the fbi worked with a company to catalog  and photograph each  item there are hundreds of things like  cell phones to key chains  that have not been returned to owners  emails and letters were sent to those  survivors on file the vegas strong  resiliency center says obtaining these  personal items will aid in the healing  process  when a tragedy like this happens they  lose that sense of safety and control  over themselves over their own person  over their  over their belongings and getting that  back gives them  a you know restores some of that control  the center is a resource and information  hub for all those impacted by the one  october shooting and it's also  very significant in having communities  do this for those that have been harmed  right it's  showing we care about you we're here for  you we're going to support you  so it definitely fosters healing if you  feel like you or a loved one have items  in the fbi's possession  you can contact the las vegas resiliency  center the center is also launching a  peer support group over the next few  months to continue to help survivors  connect with services  reporting bianca holman 8 news now
 

